Theorem PL-comp: composition theorem — the full 12-step AIMS pipeline produces a realized ArcFunction whose AimsStateMap is consistent with the pre-realization contracts, as the conjunction of the per-step ordering invariants PL-1..PL-6 and the TRMC chain PL-7..PL-11

  Preconditions:
    - The AIMS pipeline is a 12-step strictly-ordered per-function sequence
      preceded by the once-per-program interprocedural prefix (Steps 1-2)
      per Annex E §AIMS §6. PL-comp is the JOINED
      pipeline invariant: running the whole schedule on a function F yields a
      realized ArcFunction whose AimsStateMap (the converged Step-4 / Step-4a
      map consumed at realization) is consistent with the pre-realization
      interprocedural contracts (the Step-1 MemoryContract map). "Consistent"
      = no realization pass reads a summary at a stale or out-of-order
      position, the interprocedural prefix is populated before any consumer,
      and the TRMC rewrite either preserves the contract handshake or rolls
      back to a restored CFG whose recomputed summaries supersede the
      discarded rewritten ones.
    - PL-comp success-criterion (per Annex E §AIMS §6
      success_criteria #3): "Composition theorem: full 12-step pipeline
      produces a realized ArcFunction whose AimsStateMap is consistent with
      pre-realization contracts." The 13 per-step / TRMC proofs PL-1, PL-1a,
      PL-2, PL-3, PL-4, PL-4a, PL-5, PL-6, PL-7, PL-8, PL-9, PL-10, PL-11
      each discharge ONE constituent of this joined claim; none of them
      INDIVIDUALLY states the composed pipeline-wide invariant. PL-comp is
      the dedicated artifact that states the conjunction and proves it holds
      by composition.
    - PL-comp type signature (the joined obligation):
        type : Pipeline -> Bool
        running Steps 1-12 on F SHALL produce a realized ArcFunction whose
        AimsStateMap is consistent with the pre-realization contracts; the
        joined invariant holds iff every constituent ordering / staleness /
        TRMC invariant holds AND the constituent-dependency graph is acyclic
        (so the conjunction is well-founded, not circular).
    - Constituent invariants composed (the premises of PL-comp), each an
      independently-discharged §07 theorem:
        PL-1 interprocedural prefix (Steps 1-2) runs once before any
               per-function step — the contract map exists before any consumer.
        PL-1a per-function pipeline processes functions in SCC topological
               order (callees before callers) per IC-1.
        PL-2 Step 4 (analyze) precedes Step 5 (realize phase 1) — the
               AimsStateMap is produced before its first realization consumer.
        PL-3 Step 5 (realize phase 1) precedes Step 9 (merge) — position-
               keyed maps are consumed before merge invalidates them.
        PL-4 Step 10 (realize phase 2) follows Step 9 (merge) — ArcVarId-
               keyed lookups survive merge.
        PL-4a Step 8a (unwind_cleanup) precedes Step 9 (merge) — unwind CFG
               edits land before merge.
        PL-5 no pass relies on stale summaries (the umbrella sequencing
               invariant) — every summary read strictly after its latest
               production, including the Step-4a rollback re-production.
        PL-6 adding-a-pass meta-rule — any new pass preserves every ordered
               pair + updates the schedule + carries a test leg.
        PL-7 TRMC normalization detection conditions are sound.
        PL-8 TRMC candidate predicate is sound.
        PL-9 TRMC rewrite is idempotent + external arity preserved.
        PL-10 TRMC structural verification rules (a)-(e) are sufficient for
               behavioral equivalence within the constrained-rewrite scope;
               the rollback path is sound.
        PL-11 ContextBehavior initialization + componentwise join.
    - Shipped per-function driver: ori_arc::pipeline::aims_pipeline::
      run_aims_pipeline (compiler/ori_arc/src/pipeline/
      aims_pipeline/mod.rs lines 163-300) executes the schedule whose
      ordering the constituents constrain. The realized ArcFunction's
      AimsStateMap is the Step-4 / Step-4a converged map (mod.rs line 182
      bind, line 195 Step-4a rebind) consumed by Step 5 realize_rc_reuse
      (mod.rs lines 246-256) and Step 10 realize_annotations (mod.rs line 277
      + apply_phase_2_annotations). The pre-realization contracts are the
      Step-1 MemoryContract map (config.contracts, mod.rs line 187).
    - PL-comp reasons over the CONSTITUENT-DEPENDENCY graph: PL-comp's truth
      reduces to the conjunction of its 13 premises PLUS the acyclicity of
      the dependency relation among those premises. PL-5's cycle-soundness
      witness already established that the ordered-pair rules
      (PL-1/PL-1a/PL-2/PL-3/PL-4/PL-4a) feed the umbrella PL-5 acyclically
      and PL-6 is the admissibility envelope over the same schedule; PL-comp
      is the sink of that dependency tree (nothing depends on PL-comp; PL-comp
      depends on all 13). The composition adds NO new ordering claim beyond
      the conjunction — it asserts the conjunction is the realized-pipeline
      consistency property.

  Soundness property:
    Forall function F processed by run_aims_pipeline, the realized ArcFunction
    and its AimsStateMap are consistent with the pre-realization contracts iff
    the conjunction CONJ(F) of the 13 constituent invariants holds on F and the
    constituent-dependency graph G is acyclic:

      CONJ(F) = PL-1(F) AND PL-1a(F) AND PL-2(F) AND PL-3(F) AND PL-4(F)
                AND PL-4a(F) AND PL-5(F) AND PL-6(F) AND PL-7(F) AND PL-8(F)
                AND PL-9(F) AND PL-10(F) AND PL-11(F)

      (C1) Conjunction soundness:
        CONJ(F) entails the joined pipeline invariant — the interprocedural
        prefix populated before consumers (PL-1/PL-1a), the AimsStateMap
        produced before + consumed in the correct phase order
        (PL-2/PL-3/PL-4/PL-4a), no stale summary read (PL-5), the TRMC rewrite
        contract-preserving or soundly rolled back (PL-7..PL-11), and any
        future schedule edit admissibility-gated (PL-6). The realized
        AimsStateMap a downstream pass reads is therefore the converged map
        consistent with the Step-1 contracts.

      (C2) Well-foundedness (acyclicity):
        The dependency relation among the 13 constituents is acyclic — no
        constituent's discharge presupposes PL-comp, and the umbrella PL-5 +
        envelope PL-6 sit downstream of the ordered-pair rules (PL-5's
        cycle-soundness witness). The conjunction is therefore well-founded:
        PL-comp is a sink, not a circular premise.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by structural induction over the constituent-
    dependency DAG (compose the independently-discharged premises) + case
    analysis confirming the conjunction is total (every constituent present,
    none missing) and acyclic.

    Part (C1) — Conjunction soundness (structural induction over the
    constituent-dependency DAG):

      Base case — interprocedural prefix (PL-1, PL-1a):
        PL-1 discharges that Steps 1-2 run once before any per-function step
        (the MemoryContract map exists before any consumer). PL-1a discharges
        that the per-function pipeline visits functions in SCC topological
        order. Together they establish the pre-realization contract map is
        fully populated before the per-function suffix reads it — the base of
        the consistency claim.

      Inductive step — per-function ordered pairs (PL-2, PL-3, PL-4, PL-4a):
        Given the prefix base, each ordered-pair rule fixes one boundary in
        the shipped per-function schedule: PL-2 (Step 4 before Step 5), PL-3
        (Step 5 before Step 9), PL-4 (Step 10 after Step 9), PL-4a (Step 8a
        before Step 9). By the induction hypothesis the AimsStateMap producer
        precedes every consumer and the merge boundary is respected, so the
        realized map a realization pass reads is the converged map.

      Inductive step — umbrella staleness + admissibility (PL-5, PL-6):
        PL-5 composes the ordered pairs into the cross-cutting no-stale-read
        invariant (every summary read strictly after its latest production,
        including the Step-4a rollback re-production). PL-6 establishes the
        schedule is closed under admissible pass insertion. By the induction
        hypothesis the whole schedule reads non-stale summaries.

      Inductive step — TRMC chain (PL-7, PL-8, PL-9, PL-10, PL-11):
        PL-7/PL-8 establish detection + candidate soundness; PL-9 establishes
        idempotent rewrite + preserved external arity; PL-10 establishes the
        5 structural checks suffice for behavioral equivalence within the
        constrained-rewrite scope AND the rollback path is sound; PL-11
        establishes ContextBehavior init + join. By the induction hypothesis
        the TRMC rewrite either preserves the contract handshake or rolls back
        to a restored CFG whose recomputed summaries supersede the rewritten
        ones (the PL-5 rollback-supersession case). The realized AimsStateMap
        is therefore consistent with the pre-realization contracts whether or
        not TRMC fired.

      Termination:
        The 13 constituents are the complete set of §07 pipeline-ordering +
        TRMC invariants; each has been composed into the joined consistency
        claim. CONJ(F) entails the realized-pipeline consistency property.
        (C1) discharged.

    Part (C2) — Well-foundedness (case analysis on the dependency relation):

      Case ordered-pair → umbrella:
        PL-1/PL-1a/PL-2/PL-3/PL-4/PL-4a each feed PL-5 (the umbrella) and none
        depends on PL-5's output — the edges point ordered-pair → PL-5, never
        back. Acyclic.

      Case TRMC → umbrella:
        PL-10's rollback re-runs Steps 3-4 so the restored summaries supersede
        the rewritten ones — this feeds PL-5's rollback-supersession case. The
        edge points PL-10 → PL-5, never back. Acyclic.

      Case PL-comp sink:
        No constituent's discharge references PL-comp; PL-comp depends on all
        13 and nothing depends on PL-comp. PL-comp is the unique sink of the
        dependency DAG; the conjunction is well-founded. (C2) discharged.

    Coverage gate — constituent enumeration:

      The verifier re-runs each of the 13 constituent discharge routines
      (verify_pl1_interprocedural_first, verify_pl1a_scc_topological_order,
      verify_pl2_analyze_before_realize, verify_pl3_realize_before_merge,
      verify_pl4_annotations_after_merge, verify_pl4a_unwind_before_merge,
      verify_pl5_no_stale_summaries, verify_pl6_adding_a_pass_meta_rule,
      verify_pl7_trmc_detect_candidate, verify_pl8_trmc_candidate_predicate,
      verify_pl9_trmc_rewrite_idempotency, verify_pl10_trmc_structural_verify,
      verify_pl11_context_behavior_init_join) and asserts EACH returns Valid.
      A single constituent Fail makes the conjunction Fail (PL-comp is no
      stronger than its weakest premise). The verifier asserts the constituent
      count is exactly 13 (the complete §07 invariant set) so a dropped
      premise is caught as a coverage gap, not silently composed away.

      Coverage axes:
        Conjunction (C1): all 13 constituent verifiers re-run + asserted Valid.
        Well-foundedness (C2): the constituent set is the complete §07 set
          (count 13), PL-comp is a sink, the dependency DAG is acyclic per the
          PL-5 cycle-soundness witness.

    Negative-direction witness — broken constituent rejected:

      If any constituent verifier returned Fail (e.g. a hypothetical schedule
      where Step 5 reads the AimsStateMap before Step 4 produces it, failing
      PL-2 + PL-5), CONJ(F) is false and PL-comp MUST report Fail naming the
      broken constituent. The composition is exactly as strong as the
      conjunction — it never gracious-accepts over a failing premise.

    Negative-direction witness — missing constituent rejected:

      If the constituent set were incomplete (fewer than 13 premises), the
      joined invariant would be under-constrained — a pipeline boundary left
      unproven. The verifier asserts the count is 13 so a dropped premise
      fails the coverage gate rather than producing a false-valid composition.

    Cycle-soundness witness — PL-comp is the dependency sink:

      PL-comp composes PL-1..PL-11 (incl. PL-1a, PL-4a); its antecedents are
      all 13 constituents and it is the sink of the §07 dependency tree.
      No constituent depends on PL-comp, so adding PL-comp introduces no
      cycle. The dependency chain is acyclic:
        {PL-1, PL-1a, PL-2, PL-3, PL-4, PL-4a, PL-7, PL-8, PL-9, PL-10, PL-11}
          --> PL-5 / PL-6 --> PL-comp
      PL-comp is the unique sink.

