                           (mod.rs lines 163-300) — the schedule whose ordering
                           the constituents constrain; the realized AimsStateMap
                           is the Step-4/Step-4a converged map (mod.rs line 182
                           + 195) consumed at Step 5 (lines 246-256) + Step 10
                           (line 277), consistent with the Step-1 MemoryContract
                           map (config.contracts, mod.rs line 187)

    Engines dispatched:
      structural_induction (PRIMARY — structural induction over the
        constituent-dependency DAG per section_07::verify_pl_composition; the
        verifier re-runs all 13 constituent discharge routines, asserts each
        returns Valid, asserts the constituent count is exactly 13, and emits
        Fail naming the first broken or missing constituent — the composition
        is exactly as strong as the conjunction of its premises)
      case_analysis (SECONDARY — per-case grid over the constituent set +
        the acyclicity / sink check; gracious-accept once structural_induction
        has discharged the conjunction per the coverage-manifest PL row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_07 structural_induction engine discharges PL-comp by composing the 13 constituent §07 invariants (PL-1, PL-1a, PL-2, PL-3, PL-4, PL-4a, PL-5, PL-6, PL-7, PL-8, PL-9, PL-10, PL-11) — (C1) every constituent discharge routine re-runs and returns Valid so the conjunction CONJ(F) entails the realized-AimsStateMap consistency with pre-realization contracts, and (C2) the constituent set is the complete §07 set (count 13) with PL-comp the acyclic dependency sink per the PL-5 cycle-soundness witness; grounded in the shipped run_aims_pipeline driver (mod.rs lines 163-300) whose realized Step-4/Step-4a AimsStateMap is consumed at Step 5 + Step 10 consistent with the Step-1 MemoryContract map; case_analysis secondary-accepting per the coverage-manifest PL row
